+## Current peer finding: canonical collision teaching gap (proposal)
+
+The existing unresolved finding remains on generator SHA-256
+`ee0cb2856c5099e019a13201318e91bb7b4224229a6a43784ef184432b198c3e`.
+A bounded protected-Racket replay matched all three canonical demonstrations
+and the canonical query. The rival "echo only into empty destinations; preserve
+occupied originals" fits all three demonstrations, but disagrees on the query
+at zero-based `(4,1)` and `(8,5)`: native overlay swaps 4 and 9. The generator's
+`self_check` rejects that canonical query, and its constructor excludes occupied
+reflection pairs, so ordinary draws cannot teach this collision precedence.
+
+Fresh evidence: `counterexamples/peer-review-current.json`; reproducer:
+`workspace/peer_probe.py`. This confirms the retained audit without repairing or
+closing it. No production source, approval label, or review-index disposition
